  "result_text": "The diff removes the `prevWorkspaceIdRef` tracking that previously distinguished \"still in the same workspace\" from \"workspace just changed.\" Now `setSelection` at line 56-59 preserves `mode: 'new'` unconditionally whenever it was already `'new'`, with no check for whether `workspaceId` changed.\n\n**Effect:** If a user clicks \"start new session\" in workspace A, then switches to workspace B (which has existing sessions), the hook keeps `selection = { mode: 'new' }` instead of resetting and auto-selecting workspace B's most-recent session. The UI stays stuck in \"new session\" mode for the wrong workspace \u2014 `isNewSessionMode` stays true, `selectedSessionId` stays `undefined`, and `sessions[0]` for the new workspace is silently ignored, even though the comment at line 54 says \"Always select first session when sessions are available for this workspace.\"\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"packages/web-core/src/shared/hooks/useWorkspaceSessions.ts\", \"line\": 57, \"defect\": \"The workspace-change check (prevWorkspaceIdRef comparison) was deleted, so `prev?.mode === 'new'` now short-circuits regardless of whether workspaceId actually changed.\", \"effect\": \"Switching to a different workspace while in new-session mode leaves the UI stuck showing the new-session form instead of auto-selecting that workspace's most recent existing session.\"}\n```"
}
